message: "If you use this paper, its measurements, or its methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Small Decision Models: Cross-Domain Transfer Degradation — a controlled study, an AI-reviewer collaboration protocol, and a taxonomy of zero-information experiments"
abstract: >-
  A controlled empirical study of two open-source "small decision models" (Jev-class
  System One models, 395M-596M parameters) on cross-domain and cross-lingual transfer,
  based on 2,640 model forward passes on a single CPU-only machine. Reports (i) no
  detectable discriminative power on self-authored Chinese short-rule propositions
  (n=12, underpowered), (ii) a strong language effect on same-form NLI tasks verified
  by paired bootstrap dAUC tests, and (iii) that model confidence carries no information.
  Contributes three reusable methodological artifacts: three evaluation guardrails,
  an early-falsification protocol (D1-D4), and a taxonomy of three forms of
  "zero-information experiments". Also documents a two-agent (executor + independent
  AI reviewer) collaboration protocol and retains a complete ledger of the authors'
  own retracted judgments.
